    {
      "title": "Release Branches, Merge Queues and Tagging",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Release Branches, Merge Queues and Tagging",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Release branches",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`release/1.4` is cut from trunk ==only== to support old versions",
                "Fix on {green:trunk first}, then cherry-pick to the release branch",
                "`-x` appends the original sha to the commit message"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "git switch release/1.4",
                "git cherry-pick -x <sha>"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Merge queue",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "PR queued",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Rebuilt on PRs ahead",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "CI runs",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Merge to main",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Stops a ==semantic merge conflict== from breaking main",
                "Enable it in **branch protection**",
                "CI must also trigger on the `merge_group` event"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. SemVer and tags",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Change",
                "Bump",
                "1.2.3 becomes"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Breaking",
                  "**MAJOR**",
                  "2.0.0 (lower reset)"
                ],
                [
                  "Compatible feature",
                  "**MINOR**",
                  "1.3.0"
                ],
                [
                  "Bug fix",
                  "**PATCH**",
                  "1.2.4"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "git tag -a v1.4.0 -m \"Release 1.4.0\"",
                "git push origin v1.4.0"
              ],
              "note": "tags are not pushed by default"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Never move a published tag",
              "text": "Reusing or moving a published tag breaks anyone who pulled it. Ship a ==new patch== version instead."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Monorepo Pipelines with Path Filters",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Monorepo Pipelines with Path Filters",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Path filters",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Pipeline runs only when ==matching files== change",
                "Add {orange:shared deps}: `libs/`, lockfile, the workflow file itself",
                "Else dependents skip tests they need",
                "`paths-ignore: ['docs/**', '*.md']` skips CI for docs-only changes"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "yaml",
              "lines": [
                "on:",
                "  push:",
                "    paths:",
                "      - 'services/api/**'",
                "      - 'libs/shared/**'",
                "      - 'package-lock.json'",
                "      - '.github/workflows/api.yml'"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Required checks deadlock",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Required check + path filter: skipped workflow leaves the check ==pending==",
                "PR can never merge"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Detect job",
                    "sub": "always runs",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "dorny/paths-filter",
                    "sub": "what changed?",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Gated jobs",
                    "sub": "only if changed",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Per-service tags",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Tags like `api-v1.2.0` let each service ==release independently=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "yaml",
              "lines": [
                "on:",
                "  push:",
                "    tags: ['api-v*']"
              ],
              "note": "deploy trigger for the api service"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Shallow clone",
              "text": "`fetch-depth: 1` breaks change detection against the base branch. Fetch the ==diff range== (`fetch-depth: 0`)."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Cheat Sheet: Branching, Release and CI",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Cheat Sheet: Branching, Release and CI",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Trunk Daily",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "git switch -c feat/x",
                "git fetch && git rebase origin/main",
                "# squash merge the PR, then:",
                "git push origin --delete feat/x"
              ],
              "note": "branch, sync, squash merge, delete"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Branch lifetime ==under 2 days==",
                "PR under ~==400 lines==",
                "Trunk ==always green==",
                "**Trunk-based** for continuous deploy",
                "**GitFlow** only for versioned, multi-release products"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Release and SemVer",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "git tag -a v1.4.0 -m \"Release 1.4.0\"",
                "git push origin v1.4.0",
                "git cherry-pick -x <sha>  # on release/1.4"
              ],
              "note": "fix on trunk first, then cherry-pick"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Bump",
                "When"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "{red:MAJOR}",
                  "breaking change"
                ],
                [
                  "{blue:MINOR}",
                  "compatible feature"
                ],
                [
                  "{green:PATCH}",
                  "bug fix"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Published tags",
              "text": "**Never reuse or move** a published tag. Ship a new patch version."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Monorepo CI",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`paths` filter must include ==shared libs==",
                "==Always-run== change-detect job gates the rest",
                "Add the `merge_group` trigger for the ==merge queue=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A bug is found in release/1.4. A dev commits the fix only on release/1.4. What goes wrong?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Trunk never gets the fix, so 1.5 ships with the bug again.",
                "Fix on trunk first, then `git cherry-pick -x <sha>` onto the release branch."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A docs-only PR is stuck on \"Expected: waiting for status\". The CI workflow uses `paths: ['services/api/**']` and is a required check. Why, and what fixes it?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "The workflow was skipped, so the required check stays pending forever.",
                "Add an always-run change-detect job (dorny/paths-filter) that gates the downstream jobs."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Current version is 1.4.2. The next release has a bug fix and one breaking API change. What is the tag?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "`v2.0.0`: a breaking change bumps MAJOR and resets MINOR and PATCH to 0.",
                "Push it with `git push origin v2.0.0`; tags are not pushed by default."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
